1.0.0
Usage: zintrust [command] [options]

ZinTrust Framework CLI - Build production-grade TypeScript APIs

Options:
  -v, --version                                                  Output version number
  -h, --help                                                     Display help for command

Commands:
  new [options] <name>                                           Create a new ZinTrust project
  upgrade [options]                                              Upgrade an existing ZinTrust project in-place (safe, non-destructive)
  prepare [options]                                              Prepare local dist/ so it can be installed via file:/.../dist
  init:container-workers|init:cw [options]                       Initialize container-based worker infrastructure
  init:containers-proxy|init:ccp [options]                       Scaffold Cloudflare Containers proxy Worker (wrangler.containers-proxy.jsonc)
  init:proxy|init:cp [options]                                   Initialize container-based proxy stack infrastructure
  init:producer|init:p [options]                                 Configure Cloudflare Workers as producer-only
  init:ecosystem [options]                                       Scaffold docker-compose.ecosystem.yml and docker-compose.schedules.yml
  doctor:architecture|d [options]                                Validate producer/consumer architecture configuration
  add [options] <type> [name]                                    Add services and features to existing project
  create [options] <type> <name>                                 Create resources (e.g. migrations) with opinionated naming
  cm [options] <model>                                           Shortcut: create migration for a model (create_<models>_table)
  am [options] <column> <model>                                  Shortcut: add column migration for a model (add_<col>_<models>_table)
  start|s [options]                                              Start the application (dev watch, production, or Wrangler mode)
  docker|dkr [options]                                           Run Wrangler dev using a Docker-backed Cloudflare Containers config
  docker:push|docker-push [options]                              Build and push ZinTrust Docker images to Docker Hub
  queue [options] <queueName>                                    Work queued jobs (broadcast/notification)
  queue:recovery [options]                                       Run queue recovery once, start orchestrator, or recover/push a specific job
  schedule:list [options]                                        List all registered schedules
  schedule:run [options]                                         Run a specific schedule once and exit
  schedule:start [options]                                       Start schedules and keep running until SIGINT/SIGTERM
  broadcast:work [options] <queueName>                           Work queued broadcasts
  notification:work [options] <queueName>                        Work queued notifications
  resource:monitor|rm [options] <action>                         Control the resource monitor (start/stop) on the running worker service
  migrate:worker [options]                                       Run worker package migrations
  migrate [options]                                              Run database migrations
  db:seed [options]                                              Run database seeders
  d1:learn [options] <command>                                   Run a command to learn D1 queries and generate a statement registry
  d1:migrate|d1:migrate:worker [options]                         Run Cloudflare D1 migrations
  debug [options]                                                Launch debug mode with real-time monitoring dashboard
  secrets [options] [action]                                     Pull/push secrets to local .env.pull via core toolkit
  config [options] [action] [key] [value]                        Manage application configuration
  cw|container-workers [options] <action>                        Build or start container-based workers
  cp|container-proxies [options] <action>                        Build, start, or stop container-based proxy stack
  plugin|p [options]                                             Manage framework plugins
  publish:config|p:config [options]                              Publish configuration files from packages to your project
  put [options] [provider]                                       Put secrets to Cloudflare with dynamic groups from .zintrust.json
  deploy [options] [target]                                      Deploy ZinTrust to Cloudflare Workers
  deploy:ccp|deploy:containers-proxy [options]                   Deploy Cloudflare Containers proxy Worker (wrangler.containers-proxy.jsonc)
  deploy:cw|deploy:container-workers [options]                   Deploy Container Workers stack (docker-compose.workers.yml)
  deploy:cp|deploy:container-proxies [options]                   Deploy proxy stack (docker-compose.proxy.yml)
  qa [options]                                                   Run full Quality Assurance suite
  fix [options]                                                  Run automated code fixes
  key:generate [options]                                         Set the application key
  key:bulletproof|bulletproof:key [options]                      Generate/rotate BULLETPROOF_SIGNING_SECRET (signed-request proof key)
  simulate|-sim <name>                                           [INTERNAL DEV] Create a simulated ZinTrust application in simulate/ folder
  templates [options] <action> [scope] [name]                    Manage and render markdown templates (mail & notification)
  make:mail-template|make:mail [options] [name]                  Scaffold a mail markdown template into src/mail/markdown
  make:notification-template|make:notification [options] [name]  Scaffold a notification markdown template into src/notification/markdown
  routes|route:list [options]                                    List all routes (grouped by router group or service) with middleware and handler info
  jwt:dev|jwt:token [options]                                    Mint a local development JWT (for manual API testing)
  proxy [options] [target]                                       List available proxy servers
  proxy:mysql|mysql:proxy [options]                              Start the MySQL HTTP proxy for Cloudflare Workers
  proxy:postgres|postgres:proxy [options]                        Start the PostgreSQL HTTP proxy for Cloudflare Workers
  proxy:mongodb [options]                                        Start MongoDB HTTP proxy server
  proxy:sqlserver [options]                                      Start SQL Server HTTP proxy server
  proxy:redis|redis:proxy [options]                              Start the Redis HTTP proxy for Cloudflare Workers
  proxy:smtp|smtp:proxy [options]                                Start the SMTP HTTP proxy for Cloudflare Workers
  help [command]                                                 Display help for a command
